-++The generated production `docker-compose.yml` divides services across five strictly isolated Docker bridge networks:
-++1. **`edge_net`:** Connects the Caddy TLS ingress proxy to the external network and routes HTTPS traffic into the web/API service. No database or Redis containers attach to `edge_net`.
-++2. **`app_net`:** Connects the FastAPI backend service to the web client, internal caches, and the outbox event relay.
-++3. **`data_net`:** Restricted network connecting the backend service strictly to PostgreSQL 16 and Redis. Containers on `edge_net` or `sandbox_net` have zero network route to `data_net`.
-++4. **`sandbox_net`:** Air-gapped network for untrusted custom field scripts and Wasmtime runners, blocking all external egress.
-++5. **`egress_llm_net`:** Egress-only network allowing AI provider connections (OpenAI, Gemini, Ollama) and mTLS runner heartbeats on port 8444 while preventing inbound lateral movement.
