-++### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs
-++
-++- **`deployment_mode`:** Detects whether 👍kanban is executing inside a single standalone container (`standalone_embedded_pg`, typically launched via `docker run -p 8080:8080 thumbs-up-kanban:latest` with internal PostgreSQL 16) or within a compartmentalized production cluster (`production_multi_container`). In standalone mode, external Redis is optional and background tasks run in-process, whereas multi-container mode unlocks dedicated worker containers and nsjail container isolation.
-++- **`passphrase`:** The client-supplied cryptographic passphrase submitted during manual streaming backup download (`POST /api/v1/admin/standalone/backup`) and database restoration (`POST /api/v1/admin/standalone/restore`). Must be at least 16 characters in length. The server derives an AES-256-GCM symmetric key via PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 across 600,000 iterations for KBKP streaming downloads, or Argon2id for KBBAK1 archives.
-++- **`auto_backup_enabled`:** Toggles automated recurring background snapshots executed by the root-privileged `/run/postgresql/.kb_ops.sock` daemon. When enabled, the daemon captures full PostgreSQL state and object graph assets into `/var/lib/kanban/data/backups` using the timestamped `KBBAK1` format without interrupting active HTTP or WebSocket connections.
-++- **`backup_interval_hours`:** Configures the interval between automated snapshot runs. The backend permits values between 1 and 168 hours (default 24 hours). This setting determines how frequently the `/run/postgresql/.kb_ops.sock` daemon wakes to execute scheduled pg_dump snapshot routines.
-++- **`snapshot_retention_count`:** Defines the maximum number of automated snapshot `.kbbak` archives preserved within `/var/lib/kanban/data/backups` (configurable from 1 to 90, default 7). When a newly generated snapshot exceeds this threshold, the snapshot manager unlinks the oldest archives while verifying that at least the configured retention count remains accessible.
-++- **`confirm_overwrite`:** The mandatory safety gate required by the destructive database restore endpoint (`POST /api/v1/admin/standalone/restore`). The payload must contain the exact uppercase string `"RESTORE"`. Any request containing mismatched, lowercase, or omitted confirmation tokens is immediately rejected with HTTP 422 before any database sequence is touched or tables are dropped.
-++- **`backup_storage_path`:** The server-side directory where automated `.kbbak` archives reside (`/var/lib/kanban/data/backups`). This path is protected with restrictive permissions and managed exclusively by the fixed-operation socket daemon.
-++- **`compose_networks`:** The 5-network topology exported by `GET /api/v1/admin/standalone/compose-export`. Separates traffic across `edge_net` (Caddy TLS ingress), `app_net` (FastAPI backend), `data_net` (PostgreSQL 16 and Redis), `sandbox_net` (untrusted Wasm and runner execution), and `egress_llm_net` (outbound AI provider traffic). Accompanied by a secret-scrubbed `.env.example` file.
