--    "content": "# [Architectural] Universal Object Graph and Invalid Link Auditor\n\n## Overview\n\nTraditional project management databases rely on fragmented, ad-hoc foreign keys connecting tickets, documents, and attachments. This fragmented design leads to dangling pointers, orphaned files, accidental cross-tenant data leaks, and broken graph traversals when objects are archived or deleted.\n\n\ud83d\udc4dkanban resolves this through the **Universal Object Graph (UOG)**. Every major entity in the system inherits from a unified object spine, and all relationships are represented as typed, bidirectional, and audited graph links.\n\n---\n\n## The Unified Object Spine Architecture\n\nThe Universal Object Graph defines 9 first-class entity kinds (`database/models/spine.py`):\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Spine[\"Universal Object Spine<br/>- id: UUIDv7 (time-ordered monotonic)<br/>- entity_kind: Enum (9 kinds)<br/>- workspace_id: UUID (mandatory tenant boundary)<br/>- access_control_list & timestamps\"]\n    \n    Spine --> Issue[\"ISSUE\"]\n    Spine --> Doc[\"DOC\"]\n    Spine --> Sticky[\"STICKY\"]\n    Spine --> Cycle[\"CYCLE\"]\n    Spine --> Module[\"MODULE\"]\n    Spine --> View[\"VIEW\"]\n    Spine --> Page[\"PAGE\"]\n    Spine --> Project[\"PROJECT\"]\n    Spine --> Workspace[\"WORKSPACE\"]\n```\n\n![Link Graph Popover and Dependency Visualization](images/19-link-graph-popover.png)\n\n### Key Spine Invariants\n1. **Monotonic UUIDv7 Identifiers:** All objects use UUIDv7 keys, providing temporal sorting, index locality, and sub-millisecond insert performance in PostgreSQL.\n2. **Mandatory Tenant Boundary:** Every spine record requires a `workspace_id`. Cross-workspace objects cannot exist in the spine.\n3. **Canonical UTF-8 Markdown Content:** Textual representations store normalized Markdown exclusively.\n\n---\n\n## The 13 Typed Object Relationships\n\nAll inter-object relationships are stored in the centralized `object_links` table with strict referential typing:\n\n| Link Kind | Inbound Complement | Permitted Entity Pairs | Semantic Meaning |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **`BLOCKS`** | `BLOCKED_BY` | `ISSUE` -> `ISSUE` | Dependency blocker preventing completion. |\n| **`BLOCKED_BY`** | `BLOCKS` | `ISSUE` -> `ISSUE` | Dependent item waiting on prerequisite. |\n| **`RELATES_TO`** | `RELATES_TO` | Any -> Any | Non-blocking topical association. |\n| **`DUPLICATES`** | `DUPLICATED_BY` | `ISSUE` -> `ISSUE` | Identifies redundant work items. |\n| **`DUPLICATED_BY`**| `DUPLICATES` | `ISSUE` -> `ISSUE` | Original issue retained for resolution. |\n| **`PARENT_OF`** | `CHILD_OF` | `ISSUE` -> `ISSUE`, `DOC` -> `DOC` | Hierarchical parent-child composition. |\n| **`CHILD_OF`** | `PARENT_OF` | `ISSUE` -> `ISSUE`, `DOC` -> `DOC` | Sub-task or child page relationship. |\n| **`PROMOTED_TO`** | `PROMOTED_FROM`| `STICKY` -> `DOC` | Captures origin of promoted documentation. |\n| **`PROMOTED_FROM`**| `PROMOTED_TO` | `DOC` -> `STICKY` | Points back to source ideation sticky. |\n| **`MENTIONS`** | `REFERENCED_IN`| `ISSUE`/`DOC` -> Any | Inline `@mention` or object tag reference. |\n| **`REFERENCED_IN`**| `MENTIONS` | Any -> `ISSUE`/`DOC` | Backlink tracking mention occurrences. |\n| **`ATTACHED_TO`** | `DERIVED_FROM` | Media -> `ISSUE`/`DOC` | Asset or diagram attachment. |\n| **`DERIVED_FROM`** | `ATTACHED_TO` | `ISSUE`/`DOC` -> Media | Traceability to original media asset. |\n\n---\n\n## Invalid Object Link Auditor and Purger\n\nIn active development environments, soft deletes, project migrations, and permission adjustments can produce invalid relationships. Rather than allowing broken links to silently corrupt views or leak references, \ud83d\udc4dkanban runs an automated **Invalid Object Link Auditor** (`database/auditor/`).\n\n### The 6-Class Invalid Link Detection Matrix\n\nThe auditor continuously scans the `object_links` table, categorizing anomalies into 6 strict violation classes:\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    Scan[\"Auditor Background Worker\"] --> Check{\"Analyze object_links\"}\n    Check --> C1[\"1. Orphaned Source\"]\n    Check --> C2[\"2. Orphaned Target\"]\n    Check --> C3[\"3. Cross-Tenant Leak\"]\n    Check --> C4[\"4. Disallowed Self-Ref\"]\n    Check --> C5[\"5. Hierarchy Cycle\"]\n    Check --> C6[\"6. Schema Violation\"]\n    \n    C1 --> Remediate[\"Remediation Action\"]\n    C2 --> Remediate\n    C3 --> Remediate\n    C4 --> Remediate\n    C5 --> Remediate\n    C6 --> Remediate\n    \n    Remediate --> DryRun[\"--dry-run: Generate Audit Report\"]\n    Remediate --> Purge[\"--purge: Delete & Append Ledger\"]\n```\n\n1. **Orphaned Source:** The source object ID does not exist in the active object spine.\n2. **Orphaned Target:** The target object ID does not exist or has been deleted.\n3. **Cross-Tenant Leak:** The source and target objects belong to different workspaces, violating tenant isolation.\n4. **Disallowed Self-Reference:** An object links to itself in an invalid manner (e.g. `KAN-5 BLOCKS KAN-5`).\n5. **Illegal Hierarchy Cycle:** A circular dependency exists in `PARENT_OF` or `BLOCKS` graphs (e.g. A blocks B, B blocks C, C blocks A).\n6. **Schema-Violating Pair:** A link kind connects incompatible entity types (e.g. a `STICKY` claiming to `BLOCK` a `WORKSPACE`).\n\n### Audited Purging and Dry-Run Reporting\n\nPlatform administrators can inspect and remediate graph health through administrative APIs and CLI commands:\n\n```bash\n# Run link audit in dry-run mode (read-only verification)\nkanban-ctl audit-links --dry-run\n\n# Execute clean purge of corrupted links with full audit logging\nkanban-ctl audit-links --purge --reason \"Monthly maintenance cycle\"\n```\n\nAll purged links are written to the immutable `audit_ledger` with the operator ID, timestamp, and the exact violation class, ensuring forensic traceability.\n\n![Delete Blast Radius Warning Modal](images/20-delete-blast-radius.png)\n\n---\n\n## Admin Link Auditor Studio (`/admin/link-auditor`)\n\nWhile CLI commands provide automated pipeline hooks, workspace and server administrators have access to a full forensic UI studio at `/admin/link-auditor`.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Admin as Workspace / Server Admin (AAL2)\n    participant Studio as Link Auditor Studio (/admin/link-auditor)\n    participant Drawer as Inspect Link Drawer\n    participant Modal as 2-Stage Purge Modal\n    participant Engine as Auditor Engine & DB\n\n    Admin->>Studio: Navigate to /admin/link-auditor\n    Studio->>Engine: Run Integrity Scan across object_links\n    Engine-->>Studio: Return breakdown counts & keyset-paginated invalid links\n    Admin->>Studio: Click \"Inspect\" on flagged link\n    Studio->>Drawer: Open Inspect Link Drawer (source, target, violation rationale)\n    Admin->>Studio: Click \"Purge Selected Links\"\n    Studio->>Modal: Open 2-Stage Purge Confirmation Modal\n    Modal->>Admin: Require typed confirmation & reason\n    Admin->>Modal: Submit cryptographic confirmation\n    Modal->>Engine: Atomic DELETE invalid links & INSERT audit_ledger\n    Engine-->>Studio: Links purged: real-time table update\n```\n\n![Invalid Object Link Auditor Studio](images/46-admin-link-auditor.png)\n\n### 1. Six-Class Breakdown Cards\nThe top of the studio displays real-time counts across the 6 anomaly classes:\n- **Dangling Source:** Source entity does not exist in the universal object graph.\n- **Dangling Target:** Target entity does not exist or has been permanently removed.\n- **Soft-Deleted Endpoint:** Endpoint entity is marked soft-deleted while link remains active.\n- **Cross-Workspace Leak:** Link crosses workspace boundaries without multi-tenant grant.\n- **Type Matrix Violation:** Link connects object kinds prohibited by the universal type matrix.\n- **Permission Severed:** Access boundary severed between linked entities.\n\n### 2. Inspect Link Drawer\nClicking **Inspect** on any flagged row opens a detailed forensic drawer displaying full endpoint metadata, entity timestamps, link creation provenance, and specific violation details:\n\n![Inspect Link Drawer](images/47-admin-link-auditor-inspect-drawer.png)\n\n### 3. Audited Purge Modal\nTo prevent accidental data loss, purging invalid links requires two-stage administrative confirmation:\n- Displays exact count of affected links and affected entity keys.\n- Requires entering an explicit audit reason that is permanently recorded in the ledger.\n- Executes atomically inside a PostgreSQL transaction, recording SHA-256 hash-chained entries in `audit_ledger`.\n\n![Audited Purge Modal](images/48-admin-link-auditor-purge-modal.png)\n\n---\n\n## PostgreSQL Issue Copy and Subtree Graph Synthesis\n\nCloning work items, hierarchical sub-tasks, and attachments is governed by an atomic, security-definer PostgreSQL and service layer workflow (`kanban/services/issue_copy.py` and `p3_08_issue_copy.up.sql`):\n\n1. **Authorization Gate:**\n   - Requires `Capability.VIEW` (0x01) on the source issue and `Capability.EDIT` (0x04) on the target project. Missing permissions fail closed with 404 or 403.\n2. **Subtree Traversal and Fail-Closed Pruning:**\n   - Invokes `issues_get_copy_subtrees(p_root_id uuid)` (`SECURITY DEFINER`, `ltree` depth `<= 6`).\n   - Evaluates caller capability on each descendant node (`app_has_object_capability(r.id, 1)`).\n   - If an intermediate or leaf sub-issue lacks `VIEW` permission, the function prunes that node and its descendants fail-closed, aggregating pruned counts into `skipped.restricted_sub_issues` without leaking unauthorized metadata.\n3. **Safety Caps:**\n   - Enforces `MAX_READABLE_ISSUES_LIMIT = 200` to prevent unbounded memory allocation and database timeouts during tree replication.\n4. **Agent-Safe Sequence Allocation:**\n   - Calls `allocate_issue_sequences(p_project_id, p_count, false)` (`p4_24_agent_safe_sequences.up.sql`) to allocate contiguous sequence numbers atomically.\n   - Any skipped sequences are recorded with an immutable `SEQUENCE_SKIPPED` ledger event.\n5. **Atomic Savepoint Registration:**\n   - Executes inside an atomic nested transaction (`session.begin_nested()`).\n   - Cloned issues and sub-issues invoke `register_object(CAST('issue' AS object_kind), ...)` to bind spine records.\n   - Copies attachments when requested (`include_attachments=true`), links relates-to edges (`link_as_relates_to=true`), and emits `ISSUE_CREATED` and `ISSUE_COPIED` activity records.\n"
