--### The Six Defect Classes
-+![Admin Diagnostics Realtime Probe Active](images/slice4-diagnostics-realtime-probe-active.png)
- 
--```mermaid
--classDiagram
--    class ObjectLinkDefect {
--        <<enumeration>>
--        ORPHAN_SOURCE
--        ORPHAN_TARGET
--        CROSS_WORKSPACE
--        INVALID_KIND
--        INVERTED_DEPENDENCY
--        DANGLING_PARENT
--    }
--```
-+### Real-Time Diagnostics Probes
- 
--1. **`ORPHAN_SOURCE`:** The link record specifies a `source_id` entity that has been hard-deleted or does not exist in PostgreSQL.
--2. **`ORPHAN_TARGET`:** The link record specifies a `target_id` entity that no longer exists in PostgreSQL.
--3. **`CROSS_WORKSPACE`:** The link connects two entities across distinct workspace tenant boundaries without an active federation agreement, violating multi-tenant isolation.
--4. **`INVALID_KIND`:** The link record specifies an unregistered or deprecated relation kind (valid kinds: `BLOCKS`, `BLOCKED_BY`, `RELATES_TO`, `DUPLICATE_OF`, `PARENT_OF`, `CHILD_OF`).
--5. **`INVERTED_DEPENDENCY`:** An illegal cyclic or inverted dependency violates topological sort order (e.g. Issue A blocks Issue B while Issue B blocks Issue A).
--6. **`DANGLING_PARENT`:** A hierarchical child item references a parent container that has been archived, shredded, or purged.
