-+### Studio Controls and Backend Contracts
-+
-+The Migration Import Studio exposes dedicated endpoints for each platform: `POST /api/v1/admin/imports/plane`, `POST /api/v1/admin/imports/jira`, `POST /api/v1/admin/imports/github`, and `POST /api/v1/admin/imports/linear`:
-+
-+1. **Source Platform Tabs:**
-+   Selects the target parser and schema mapping logic for the submitted export payload (`Plane`, `Jira`, `GitHub Issues`, or `Linear`). Selecting a source automatically configures the appropriate entity mapping pipeline and CommonMark converters.
-+
-+2. **Target Workspace and Project (`workspace_slug`, `project_key`):**
-+   Specifies the destination tenant and project key for all imported entities. If omitted, the importer creates or binds to the default workspace and project declared inside the bundle. Imported issues receive canonical sequence numbers under the target project key (e.g. `KAN-1`, `KAN-2`).
-+
-+3. **Dry-Run Simulation Toggle (`dry_run`):**
-+   When enabled (`dry_run=true`), the importer executes a non-destructive simulation against a database savepoint. It calculates entity diff counts, validates referential links, checks user mappings, and generates an `ImportDiffReport` without committing rows to PostgreSQL. When disabled (`dry_run=false`), the import runs inside an atomic database transaction that commits only upon full validation success.
-+
-+4. **Custom User Mapping JSON (`user_map`):**
-+   A JSON dictionary mapping source usernames, legacy IDs, or email addresses to canonical 👍kanban user accounts (e.g. `{"legacy_user": "adamoutler@gmail.com", "usr_123": "engineer@example.com"}`). Unmapped users fall back to the system administrator or are created as external inactive principals depending on organizational configuration.
-+
-+5. **Legacy Key Alias Preservation (`IssueKeyAlias`):**
-+   Whenever legacy issues are imported from Jira, GitHub, or Linear, their historical keys (e.g. `JIRA-101`, `GH-88`, `ENG-42`) are automatically recorded in the `issue_key_aliases` catalog. For API clients querying `GET /api/v1/issues/{issue_key}`, the server returns `200 OK` JSON with the header `X-Kanban-Canonical-Key: {canonical_key}`. For browser navigation where `Accept` includes `text/html` (and not `application/json`), the server returns `HTTP 308 Permanent Redirect` with `Location: /projects/{project_key}/issues/{canonical_key}`.
