-+### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs
-+
-+- **`per_source_endpoints`:** Ingestion is executed via 4 distinct per-platform endpoints: `POST /api/v1/admin/imports/plane` (Plane workspace JSON), `POST /api/v1/admin/imports/jira` (Jira Cloud/Server JSON or REST dump with ADF support), `POST /api/v1/admin/imports/github` (GitHub Issues REST/CLI JSON), and `POST /api/v1/admin/imports/linear` (Linear JSON archive). Each parser normalizes rich text into sanitized UTF-8 CommonMark while strictly rejecting Unicode lone surrogates.
-+- **`workspace_slug` and `project_key`:** Defines the destination tenant context and issue key prefix for the imported dataset. If specified, issues are allocated sequential integer sequence IDs under the destination project key (e.g. `KAN-1`, `KAN-2`). If left empty, the importer provisions or resolves the workspace and project names specified within the input bundle.
-+- **`dry_run`:** Controls whether database modifications are committed. When set to `true`, the importer runs within a PostgreSQL `SAVEPOINT`, parses all entities, validates foreign keys, checks user mappings, and emits an `ImportDiffReport` before rolling back the savepoint. When set to `false`, the operation executes within an atomic database transaction that commits only upon 100% validation success.
-+- **`user_map`:** A JSON dictionary mapping source account identifiers, legacy usernames, or email addresses to canonical 👍kanban user accounts (e.g. `{"legacy_dev": "alice@example.com"}`). Unmapped accounts fall back to system defaults, ensuring that ownership, assignments, and historical comments remain traceable.
-+- **`legacy_key_aliases`:** Upstream issue keys (such as `JIRA-101`, `GH-88`, `ENG-42`) are automatically extracted and recorded in the `issue_key_aliases` catalog. When queries arrive for obsolete keys (`GET /api/v1/issues/{issue_key}`), API clients receive `200 OK` JSON with header `X-Kanban-Canonical-Key: {canonical_key}`, while browser requests requesting `text/html` receive `HTTP 308 Permanent Redirect` with `Location: /projects/{project_key}/issues/{canonical_key}`.
-+- **`export_workspace_slug` and `export_scrub`:** Used by the portable workspace exporter (`POST /api/v1/admin/exports/portable`) to generate a compressed `.tar.gz` bundle. When `scrub=true` (`export_scrub` in UI), secret patterns and authentication tokens are actively redacted from prose fields before packaging.
